-- title:
--   Adjoin of commuting semisimple endomorphisms: semisimple and reduced
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a perfect field and $V$ a finite-dimensional $K$-vector space, and let $s$ be a set of $K$-linear endomorphisms of $V$. Assume that the elements of $s$ commute pairwise, i.e. $xy = yx$ for all $x, y \in s$, and that each $x \in s$ is semisimple in the sense of `Module.End.IsSemisimple`, namely that $V$, viewed as a module over $K[X]$ with $X$ acting by $x$, is a semisimple module (equivalently, the minimal polynomial of $x$ is squarefree). The conclusion is a conjunction: first, every element $a$ of the $K$-subalgebra $\operatorname{Algebra.adjoin} K\, s \subseteq \operatorname{End}_K(V)$ generated by $s$ is again semisimple in this sense; second, that subalgebra, regarded as a ring in its own right, is reduced, i.e. its only nilpotent element is $0$. No commutativity or semisimplicity hypothesis beyond the two stated is imposed, and $s$ is an arbitrary (possibly infinite) set.
--
--   This is the standard statement that a commuting family of semisimple endomorphisms over a perfect field generates a semisimple, hence reduced, commutative subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_K(V)$. In the present development it serves as the source of reducedness for Hecke algebras generated by commuting semisimple Hecke operators: it is cited by [`CuspForm.TWLevel.HeckeRing.isReduced`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.HeckeRing.isReduced) and by [`CohCarrier.exists_squarefree_aeval_heckeTL_mem_parabolicHoms`](thm.html#CohCarrier.exists_squarefree_aeval_heckeTL_mem_parabolicHoms).
-- source:
